<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, maximum-scale=1.0, user-scalable=no" />

  <title>AI forum</title>

  <link rel="stylesheet" href="reset.css" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="reveal.css" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="black.css" />

  <!-- Theme used for syntax highlighted code -->
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="monokai.css" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="mystyle.css" />
</head>

<body>
  <div class="reveal">
    <div class="slides">
      <!-- ******************** TITLE SLIDE ********************** -->
      <section data-hide-slide-number="true" data-background-image="images/clouds.png"
        data-transition="zoom">
        <h1 style="text-shadow: 5px 5px 10px black; margin-top:200px">
          AI forum: Research group Bernauer
        </h1>
        
        <div style="margin-bottom: 100px">July 16th, 2026</div>
        <center>
          <img style="height: 250px; vertical-align: -100px; margin-right: 100px"
            src="images/cfns_logo_2018.png" />
          <img style="height: 300px; vertical-align: -150px; margin-right: 100px"
            src="images/SBUlogo.png" />
        </center>

        
      </section>

      
      

      <section data-background-image="images/puzzle.jpg">
        <h1>What we do/have</h1>
        <div>
        <h2>MUSE</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Beam line Calorimeter reconstruction:  CNN + BDTs</li>
            <li>Straw Tube tracking/seeding: GNN (beginning)    </li>
        </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
        <h2>DarkLight</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Focal-plane to target transfer: DNN, BDTs</li>
            <li>Direct GEM ADC to target: DNN $\rightarrow$ out-perfoms traditional methods</li>
        </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
        <h2>MLLM: Machine Learning Learning Machine</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Postdoc-initiated CFNS/HEP "journal club"</li>
            <li>Good for exchange of ideas, getting into AI</li>
        </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
        <h2>Existing hardware</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Storage + Compute server with ca 100TB disks, 5090</li>            
        </ul>
        </div>
     </section>

  
 <section data-background-image="images/puzzle.jpg">
        <h1>What we are planning to do</h1>
        <div>
        <h2>Foundation Models for Transferable Particle Tracking</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>A model that <hl>understands</hl> tracks</li>
            <li>Based on FM4NPP </li>
            <li>Multi-modal: Different detector types with different information content</li>
            <li>Multi-experiment: Different geometries. Here: sPHENIX, DarkLight, MUSE (Seaquest)</li>
            <li>Raw detector information: Avoid information loss in hit building</li>
        </ul>
        <h3> Tasks</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Data preparation and ingestion</li>
            <li>Model architecture development</li>
            <li>Training and scaling studies</li>
            <li>Cross-experiment validation and deployment</li>
        </ul>
           <h3> Support</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>2 postdocs for 9 month</li>
            <li>6 month graduate student</li>
            <li>Ca 70k for AI server</li>
            
        </ul>
        <div>
            (SBU: JCB (Lead Pi), Axel; Argonne: Paul Reimer; BNL: Yeonju G, Yi Huang)
        </div>
        </div>
        
    </section>

  
 <section data-background-image="images/puzzle.jpg">
        <h1>Some thoughts on department hardware</h1>
        <div>
        <h2>Three stages of scale</h2>
        <ol>
            <li>Laptop / normal PC: $\rightarrow$ Consumer-level GPU</li>
            <li>Single compute server: $\rightarrow$ 1 to few professional GPUs</li>
            <li>Distributed: $\rightarrow$ Multi-Node with multi-GPUs</li>            
        </ol>
        <h2>Three stages of development</h2>
        <ol>
            <li>Prototyping: 1-2</li>
            <li>Scale up tests: 2</li>
            <li>Full run: 2-3</li>            
        </ol>
        <div style="margin-top:30px">
        <hl>Most of us have 1.</hl> <hl2>Clusters/HPC are available for 3.</hl2> <hl3>2 is the bottleneck.</hl3>
</div>
<div style="margin-top:30px">
        <em>But we need not only compute, we also need storage!</em>
       
</div>
<div style="margin-top:30px">
    Per project: Compute is short-term peaky, but storage is long-term. Moving data is slow. 
</div>
    </section>


      

    </div>
  </div>

  <script src="reveal.js"></script>
  <script src="highlight.js"></script>
  <script type="text/javascript" src="https://cdn.bokeh.org/bokeh/release/bokeh-3.2.2.min.js"></script>
  <script type="text/javascript" src="https://cdn.bokeh.org/bokeh/release/bokeh-widgets-3.2.2.min.js"></script>
  <script type="text/javascript">
    Bokeh.set_log_level("info");
  </script>
  <script>
    window.resizeTo(1920, 1200);

    // More info about initialization & config:
    // - https://revealjs.com/initialization/
    // - https://revealjs.com/config/
    Reveal.initialize({
      hash: true,
      width: 1920,
      height: 1200,
      margin: 0.04,
      slideNumber: false,
      controls: false,
      progress: false,
      transition: "fade",
      center: false,
      preloadIframes: true,
      viewdistance: 30,
      backgroundTransition: "fade",
      // Learn about plugins: https://revealjs.com/plugins/
      plugins: [
        RevealMarkdown,
        RevealHighlight,
        RevealNotes,
        RevealMath.KaTeX,
      ],
    });
    Reveal.addEventListener("slidechanged", (event) => {
      const isSnOn = event.currentSlide.dataset.hideSlideNumber !== "true";
      Reveal.configure({ slideNumber: isSnOn });
    });
  </script>
</body>

</html>